Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-09-2000||10:43 PM||||  Allright, I hate to admit it but,I "DON'T" know the difference between a front stabilizer bar and a sway bar. Could someone please help. I can't believe it myself; sorry if I wasted your time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">.<P> Thanx, bam-bam  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Oreif||04-09-2000||11:22 PM||||Stabilizer bar is a sway bar (anti-sway bar).<BR>They are the same item just different name. Like honda and toyota each is named different but still a rice burner  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Or "a rose by any other name is but a rose"<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||04-10-2000||09:43 AM||||Would, "If it walks like a duck and talks like a duck..." fit??||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||04-10-2000||04:02 PM||||The front sway bar is a piece of metal rod that connects the two front lower control arms together. The front steering stabilizer looks like a shock absorber that attaches to the steering rack.||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||04-10-2000||04:16 PM||||... a Platypus?  Right, MM?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||04-10-2000||04:17 PM||||so what does the stabilizer/shock absorber do ? <P>are all fieros so equiped?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||gixxer||04-10-2000||07:41 PM||||The stabilizer that the Batboy is referring to is the steering damper, I believe. It cuts down on road shock or "kick back" thru the steering wheel when the tires pass over a nasty section of road. Most cars don't have one, but most cars aren't mid-engined either. <BR>Isn't suspension terminology great?<BR>Everybodys definition of "stabilizer" is valid too, in my experience.<BR>So,"stabiliser" can mean:<BR>1)sway bar<BR>2)anti roll bar<BR>3)anti sway bar<BR>4)steering damper<BR>Anybody got any more?||||reg||6
Z||000007||BAM-BAM||04-10-2000||08:13 PM||||   Thanks guys, now I feel enlightened. Thank you all for your time and input.<P>  BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000008||batboy||04-10-2000||08:46 PM||||I stand corrected, the Haynes manual says the steering shock thingy is called a steering damper too.||||reg||1
